# ezacto-oss — local dev secrets (copy to .dev.vars; NEVER commit .dev.vars)
# Infrastructure bindings (D1 database, R2 receipts/exports, Queues) are wrangler
# bindings, not env vars — they live in wrangler.jsonc when the worker entry lands.

# --- Identity seam: Cloudflare Access implementation (D4) ---
# Optional pair. Leave both empty to disable. The team domain must be the exact
# origin form https://your-team.cloudflareaccess.com (without a trailing slash).
ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
ACCESS_POLICY_AUD=

# --- Browser identity: provider-generic OIDC with Google configured first ---
# These values must be present as a pair. Use a dedicated Web client per live
# environment; local sign-in needs an HTTPS APP_BASE_URL registered as a callback.
OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
OIDC_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=

# --- Mailer seam: AWS SES HTTP API (D14 / issue #46) ---
# Credentials are secrets. Prefer short-lived credentials plus a session token
# where the deployment environment can rotate them. Never commit real values.
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=
# Static routing/configuration. The sender identity and its DKIM records must be
# verified in this exact region. Configuration-set events are provisioned in AWS.
SES_REGION=us-west-2
SES_FROM=Ezacto <notify@example.test>
SES_CONFIGURATION_SET=ezacto-events

# --- App ---
# OIDC callbacks require HTTPS. Use an HTTPS local tunnel when exercising OIDC.
APP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8787
SESSION_SECRET=
# Canonical unpadded base64url encoding of exactly 32 random bytes. Keep the same
# value across releases or outstanding API cursors become invalid.
API_CURSOR_SIGNING_KEY=
# One-time operator credential. Install only while running instance bootstrap;
# remove it from the Worker immediately after the owner token is verified.
EZACTO_BOOTSTRAP_TOKEN=

# --- Accounting mirror: QuickBooks (issue #104) ---
# Optional pair; without both the QuickBooks routes are not mounted. The webhook
# verifier comes from the webhooks page in the Intuit portal; without it no
# delivery is accepted.
QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_ID=
QUICKBOOKS_CLIENT_SECRET=
QUICKBOOKS_WEBHOOK_VERIFIER_TOKEN=
# `sandbox` reaches Intuit's test companies. Anything else, including empty, is
# LIVE BOOKS.
QUICKBOOKS_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox

# --- Payouts: a contractor's own Wise account, by OAuth (issue #543) ---
# Optional pair; leave both empty and the Wise routes are not mounted at all, so
# a contractor sees no connect button rather than one that fails at the consent
# screen. Register the callback as
# <APP_BASE_URL>/api/v1/integrations/wise/callback in the Wise app.
WISE_CLIENT_ID=
WISE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# `sandbox` reaches Wise's test accounts. ANYTHING ELSE, INCLUDING EMPTY, IS
# LIVE — the safe way round, because a live token against sandbox is refused
# loudly where a sandbox token against live looks like a payout that went
# nowhere.
WISE_ENVIRONMENT=sandbox
# The PEM Wise signs webhook deliveries with, for the subscription pointed at
# <APP_BASE_URL>/webhooks/wise. Optional on sandbox -- Wise's published sandbox
# key is used -- and REQUIRED on live: an unverifiable claim about money is
# refused rather than trusted, so live deliveries are rejected until this is set.
WISE_WEBHOOK_PUBLIC_KEY=
# Where Wise is, for a SANDBOX deployment only -- both or neither, and ignored
# on live, which is always Wise's own address. There is no default: Wise
# decommissioned api.sandbox.transferwise.tech (it answers 410) and no
# replacement hostname is guessed here, so a sandbox deployment without these is
# reported as not configured rather than quietly calling an address that is gone.
WISE_API_BASE=
WISE_AUTHORIZE_URL=

# --- migrate package (dev, against the live Harvest account) ---
HARVEST_ACCOUNT_ID=
HARVEST_PAT=
HARVEST_USER_AGENT_EMAIL=
